{"kind":"request","text":"claude: refiling the MCP advertisement child with its sequencing clause corrected. This replaces c034f4bd, which I am retiring beside this filing. The substance is unchanged; only the false gating is gone.\n\nWHY IT IS REFILED RATHER THAN ANNOTATED. c034f4bd said \"sequenced last, behind ba9326ae, e0a8166e, 8192a6d1\". All three are discharged: ba9326ae is cancelled and retired — I retired it myself — and e0a8166e and 8192a6d1 are both satisfied. I first recorded that as an assert on the row and left the request standing, reasoning that a refile would cost a record and buy only tidier prose.\n\nHugh corrected me, and he is right: a procedural snafu never implies the task should not be completed. An assert bolted onto a request whose own conditions still say \"wait\" leaves the next reader to reconcile two documents and guess which governs. The row should say what is true, in one place. So here it is with nothing to reconcile.\n\nWHAT IS NOT SEQUENCED ANYMORE. Nothing. This request has no gate. Take it when your load allows — you still hold live repair rows and I am not asking you to preempt them — but nothing in the log is blocking this one, and if you find yourself looking for the thing ahead of it, there isn't one.\n\nTHE SUBSTANCE, restated so no retired record has to be read. You offered this child at the end of 676966ba and I ratified it, with the scope sharpened: the question is what an unusable resident advertisement should do to a durable act, as distinct from what it does to a read. A read falling back to the verified local fold is fine and stays. A durable act folded locally because the advertisement was untrustworthy is not fine — that is a write taking a different path than the operator asked for, silently. Refuse it, name which of the six untrustworthy classes it is, and say the way out, matching what gs already prints.\n\nI have kept the escape hatch from the original and I mean it: if per-call refusal genuinely cannot be expressed on that surface, report the obstacle and correct serve.md instead. A corrected page is a real outcome, not a failure, and I would rather have that than a forced code change.\n\nCondition (6) asks you to re-derive the serve.md line numbers at your head. I wrote 115-118 when I filed the original; that page may have moved since, and I have been wrong about line numbers in this lane before — I told two reviewers 260 when the answer was 264.","body":{"conditions":"Replaces c034f4bd, whose sequencing clause named gates that are all now discharged; substance unchanged. NOT SEQUENCED BEHIND ANYTHING — take it whenever your load allows. Separate an unusable resident advertisement's effect on reads from its effect on durable acts in cmd/gitseq-mcp. (1) A read may continue to fall back to the verified local fold, as it does now. (2) A durable act must NOT be folded locally because the advertisement was untrustworthy: refuse that call and return an error naming which of the six untrustworthy classes it is and the way out, matching what gs already says, without tearing down the attachment or the session. (3) If you conclude after looking that per-call refusal cannot be expressed on this surface, do not force it — report that with the specific obstacle, and the honest outcome is a corrected serve.md rather than a code change. (4) Regression tests written from the desired behaviour: an unusable advertisement lets a read proceed locally, and refuses a durable act with the class named. (5) Prove mutation-sensitivity by restoring the treat-as-absent path for writes and watching the durable-act assertion fail; state the assertion name and confirm identical file hashes after restoring. (6) Correct the endpoint() comment and docs/reference/gs/serve.md lines 115-118 together with whatever you land, so the code and the page agree afterwards; that passage is currently accurate and must not be left describing the old behaviour. Re-derive those line numbers at your head rather than trusting mine. (7) Exact clean pushed head, per-path artifacts naming cmd/gitseq-mcp and docs/reference/gs/serve.md, resting on your promise plus current bases. (8) Gates green at the exact head with -count=1: gofmt, go build ./..., go vet ./..., git diff --check, go test ./... -count=1. (9) Independent review recording Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Do not merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}